{
  "name": "50 · CEO Agent (Kaamchor AI · MAP 3.0)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 50 · CEO Agent\nYour AI CEO. Message it on WhatsApp or Telegram (\"aaj ka business kaisa hai?\", \"kaun leave pe hai?\", \"Diwali offer bhejo\") → it decides which of your **7 teams** to call, runs those workflows, and replies with one short answer. It always asks you before anything is sent to customers. Every morning at 8 AM it also sends you yesterday's numbers.\n\n**Setup (30 min)**\n1. For each team you want, open a workflow of that department (e.g. 28 Daily Cash for Finance), add a **When Executed by Another Workflow** trigger with one input `request`, and make its last node return the answer as text. Copy that workflow's ID (from its URL) into the matching tool: YOUR_SALES_WORKFLOW_ID, YOUR_SUPPORT_WORKFLOW_ID, ... Delete tools you don't need.\n2. AI model node: add an **Anthropic** credential (or swap the model node for OpenAI / Gemini).\n3. WhatsApp nodes: add a **WhatsApp Business Cloud API** credential and replace YOUR_PHONE_NUMBER_ID with your Phone Number ID (Meta → WhatsApp → API setup). Replace YOUR_OWNER_WHATSAPP with the owner's WhatsApp number in 91XXXXXXXXXX format.\n4. Telegram nodes: add a **Telegram API** credential (bot token from @BotFather) and replace YOUR_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID.\n5. Google Sheets nodes: add a **Google Sheets OAuth2** credential and paste your sheet link in place of YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_URL. Tabs: Leads, Sales, Expenses, Tickets, Tasks, Stock (same sheet as your other agents).\n\nOnly the owner's number / chat ID can talk to it. Use one WhatsApp trigger per Meta app (see README tips).",
        "height": 847,
        "width": 440,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "4da1df84-893d-447a-a5e5-51a8b1b70d9e",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -520,
        -180
